                <pb facs="0965" n="651" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg651"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111/1404a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to all Seaport Consuls </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1915-01-11">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">January 11, 1915</hi>.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Circular telegram]</p>
                <p>You need not report further in response to circular instructions of November
                        22<anchor n="6" xml:id="d1042-f1"/> and following relative to unneutral
                    service, except in suspicious cases. You will not, however, relax your vigilance
                    to obtain and report information regarding violations of American neutrality and
                    transshipment of cargoes at sea to belligerent warships.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
